
What is Spring Boot?

Spring Boot is an open-source, Java-based framework used to build standalone, production-ready applications with minimal effort. It is built directly on top of the traditional Spring Framework
Core Features 
• Auto-Configuration: It automatically configures your application based on the dependencies you add. For example, if you add a database dependency, Spring Boot configures the database connection automatically.
• Opinionated 'Starter' Dependencies: Instead of manually searching for and matching compatible library versions, you can use "starter" packs (like spring-boot-starter-web). These bundle all required dependencies into a single, verified package.
• Embedded Servers: It includes built-in servers like Tomcat or Jetty. This means you can package your application into a single .jar file and run it directly anywhere, without needing to install an external web server

-   Spring boot is a spring based framework which is open source and developed by Pivotal Team.
-   Spring Boot provides AutoConfiguration which means reduce Common lines of code in Application which is written by Programmers and handles Jars with version management. (i.e. Providing Configuration code XML/Java and maintaining all jars required for Project Parent Jars + Child Jars)
